WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.569
-Our first guest tonight
an Emmy Award-winning comedian

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:07.607
in his record-setting 19th
season on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.275
You can also see him in "Kenan,"

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.544
which airs Monday nights
at 8:00 here on NBC.

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.512
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.380
-Don't do it.
-Do what?

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.448
-Don't you lock me
in this basement again

00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:18.584
like when we was kids.
-Man, would I try to do that?

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:19.953
I'm grown.
I'm a grown-ass man now.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.053
-Stop inching towards the steps.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:22.288
-I ain't inchin' towards
none of them.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.256
Grown man!
-Stop inchin'!

00:00:24.256 --> 00:00:26.693
-I don't got to do
nothing you say.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:31.497
-Gary! Gary!

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:32.965
Ow!

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:34.801
Boy, if I catch you!

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.402
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.838
our very good friend
Kenan Thompson, everybody.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.807
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:47.914 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:54.987 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:54.987 --> 00:01:02.094 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:03.963
Welcome back, my friend.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.465
Welcome back.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.634
-That was a funny clip.
That was a pretty funny clip.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.170
-Really funny clip.
-I'm proud of that.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.772
-19 years on "SNL."

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.240
I feel like "SNL"
is one of those shows,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.642
it maybe gets a little easier
but it never gets easy, right?

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:19.245
-No. I mean, you know,
it's comedy.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.314
I think comedy has to be earned
every single time.

00:01:22.314 --> 00:01:23.983
You can't just assume that

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.684
everybody's going to laugh,
like now.

00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:26.885
[ Laughter ]
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:26.885 --> 00:01:28.187
-But now, tell me,
I was wondering,

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.123
'cause now this is the second
year of double duty,

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.790
where you've done "SNL"
at the same time

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:32.791
you're filming "Kenan."
-Yeah.

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:34.059
-Season 2 of "Kenan,"

00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:35.495
you've got a really great cast.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.229
You got Don Johnson.
Chris Redd from the clip.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:38.998
Fortune Feimster.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.933
What do you think?
Is it like one season

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.203
of a sitcom is equal
to like 10 years of "SNL"?

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.504
How do you feel in year two?

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.072
Do you feel, like,
way more settled?

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.707
-It is a lot. It's a very
different experience.

00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:50.476
Like "SNL," we can kind of just,
you know,

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:52.545
coast it out a little bit
until Saturday,

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:56.649
you know, because the show is
live, so the only kind of things

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.051
that we really do for real
are the pre-tapes on Fridays.

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:01.187
So Monday through Thursday
I'm just in, like,

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:04.090
sweats and,
you know, dirty socks.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.424
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:08.294
But when we shoot, when I show
up on the "Kenan" set,

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:11.164
it's like a 12-hour day,
for sure, guaranteed.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.032
It's like that
Monday through Friday.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.903
So, yeah, it takes a lot,
but at the same time,

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.305
it's such a wonderful group of
people, like you just said.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.840
Also Kimrie Lewis
and Taylor Louderman,

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.542
and Dani and Dannah,
my little daughters.

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:25.578
It's a just great group
of people.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.580
-So, Dani and Dannah,
who play your daughters,

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.383
they are real-life sisters?
-Yeah, real-life sisters.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.418
-And you got started --
Here they are right there.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.253
-Look at -- They're sweethearts.
[ Audience aws ]

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:36.956
Look at their sweet faces.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.458
-And now, you obviously
got started

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:41.961
in this game as a young person.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.630
-Yeah, but not that young,
and imagine to be able to

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.532
start your experience
with your sibling.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.734
I think it's such a great story.
-Yeah.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.135
-And they are from Atlanta
as well,

00:02:50.135 --> 00:02:51.704
so they are keeping it very real
on the show.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.372
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:56.576
-Was Georgia winning
the national championship,

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.444
was that a big deal?
-Bulldogs, yeah.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.812
Shout-out to the Bulldogs!

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.046
Where the South at? Bible belt!

00:03:01.046 --> 00:03:03.983
-How was your mom with it?

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:09.254
-My mom, she is a big fan but
she's more of an Ohio State fan.

00:03:09.254 --> 00:03:10.523
-Okay, gotcha.
-Unfortunately,

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.790
she went to Ohio State.
[ Light boos ]

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.959
I know, right?
Midwest, nah, no thanks.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:18.665
-By the way,
if you met Kenan's mom

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.767
and you just booed her school...

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.268
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.203
The sweetest woman!
-She is a very sweet woman.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.806
I didn't know where you were
going with that.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.975
-You were like trying to decide
if you were gonna have my back?

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.976
You were like, either
"listen to him" or like --

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:33.445
[ Laughter ]
-"Take it easy, Seth."

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:34.980
Attacking his own audience.
-I thought of you this week.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.683
I mean, I was very happy about
this as a Red Sox fan.

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:41.487
David Ortiz, "Big Papi," got
inducted into the Hall of Fame.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.389
It is, and I mean, a long list,

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.457
but this is my favorite
of your impressions.

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:48.761
-Oh, my God, he's saying
"biiig lunch."

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:51.597
That's what he's going to have
to celebrate, a biiig lunch.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:54.199
Big Papi, yeah.
I love that dude.

00:03:54.199 --> 00:03:56.702
-Did you see him
find out the news?

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:57.904
I mean, because the only thing
I'll say is --

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:00.706
-Very casual, like he wasn't
expecting it.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:02.742
-The great thing about it,
first of all, I loved his shirt.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.411
-Full dinner party.
Yeah, colorful.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.379
-I don't know if the sound
was synced wrong,

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.281
because the thing I liked about
it, he was on the phone

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:11.417
with a guy for a really long
time before he celebrated

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.951
getting the news,
and it was very clear

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:14.220
where the call was going.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.256
-Also I felt like they all heard
it before he celebrated,

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.291
so they were just waiting on him
patiently.

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:21.927
Shout-out to them because they
were very poised.

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.529
-I felt like everybody else
in the room was like,

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.397
"David, you know
they're saying yes?"

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:27.199
-Also, Cooperstown,

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:29.268
who's calling with something
else, you know?

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:31.403
There's no other news.

00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:33.071
-They're like, "Hi, David.
This is Cooperstown.

00:04:33.071 --> 00:04:34.373
Are you with people?"
"I am."

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.242
He's like, "Uh, maybe go
in the other room."

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.211
[ Laughter ]
-"You didn't get it."

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:41.480
"Well, why would you call?"

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.449
-How was it having our friend
Will Forte back last week?

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:45.952
-Yes, it was the best.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.987
I mean, and shout-out
to Ariana DeBose.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:50.256
She did an incredible job
the week before.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.558
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:56.595
But it's always such a pleasure
when our old people

00:04:56.595 --> 00:04:58.363
come back
and I can take the week off.

00:04:58.363 --> 00:05:00.099
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:04.704
But, like, Forte had basically
like 80% of the show written

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.071
already before he came
through the door,

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:07.272
so it was just incredible.

00:05:07.272 --> 00:05:08.374
And then Kristen was back.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:11.244
It was great to see
Kristen around.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:14.680
-You have some people
who you impersonate.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.615
You mentioned Big Papi.

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:18.951
You did this this week,
and Stephen Smith saw it.

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.252
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:22.788
-Yeah, Michael Irvin.
-You did a Michael Irvin.

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:25.658
This didn't even air.
This just went up online.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.893
-That means Stephen A. Smith
really did it.

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:29.695
That's really cool.

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:33.399
Yeah, me and Chris and Chloe did
their morning show,

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:37.136
so it was me doing Michael Irvin
and Stephen A. was Chris,

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:41.374
and Chloe was -- I don't
remember the lady's name.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:44.109
"The lady," unfortunately.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:46.245
-No, that's fine. In this day
and age, that's fine.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.747
-Yeah, there's going to be some
friendly tweets about that

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:50.816
to be answered tonight,
I'm sure.

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:54.287
But, yeah, it's always nice
when people can take

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:56.389
the impersonation in stride,
and they loved it

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.223
and they shouted it out,
so it was great.

00:05:58.223 --> 00:05:59.992
-You got a shout-out.

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:01.761
-Now I'm Googling
who that lady is.

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:04.230
-Okay, great, and then we can --
-We'll continue to talk.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.298
Go ahead.
-We'll ADR it in later, yeah.

00:06:06.298 --> 00:06:09.001
I'll make this question
a long setup.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.470
-"First Take lady."
-So, "Weekend Update"

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.172
is a segment,
it's sort of a news parody.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:14.806
It happens in the middle
of the show.

00:06:14.806 --> 00:06:15.841
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.841 --> 00:06:17.710
-Colin Jost, Michael Che.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.112
Molly Qerim. That's her name.
Yeah, Molly.

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:22.047
So Chloe played Molly.
Shout-out to Molly.

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:25.551
-Thank you. Shout-out to Molly.
We apologize.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.854
So, you guys did
the Village People.

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:29.555
-This was such
a fun "Weekend Update"

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:32.658
because it just
came out of the blue.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.626
I don't think it had anything
to do with, like,

00:06:34.626 --> 00:06:36.828
what most of that "Update"
was about that week.

00:06:36.828 --> 00:06:38.730
I think it was the anniversary
of the song or something.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.366
-I think it was maybe that Trump
was using it

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:41.533
as his walk-in music.
-That's what it was.

00:06:41.533 --> 00:06:43.569
Trump was using it
as his campaign music

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.804
without permission,
and they did not like that.

00:06:45.804 --> 00:06:50.209
So we did this sketch,
and then I got to get a chance

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.977
to meet Victor,
the guy I was playing.

00:06:51.977 --> 00:06:55.047
He called and was like --
I think his assistant called,

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:56.315
and was like, "Would you like to
meet Victor?"

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.950
I was like, "I'm sorry, who?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.520
"You remember you did
the Village People yesterday?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.556
And Victor saw it, and he would
like to Zoom with you guys."

00:07:04.556 --> 00:07:06.893
I was like, "Of course."
I got Bowen to come.

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.995
We were just sitting there
on a Zoom,

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:12.564
which are usually pretty casual,
but Victor's side of the Zoom

00:07:12.564 --> 00:07:15.901
was very hoity-toity,
to a point.

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:18.638
I mean, it was just
a sheet curtain background.

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:20.005
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.005 --> 00:07:22.240
It was a lot of anticipation.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:23.743
"Please hold for Victor."

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.777
And then he came into frame,

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:30.516
full helmet and sunglasses
and the whole nine.

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:34.687
I was an immediate --
I could have been in 1975.

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:36.021
-Yeah.

00:07:36.021 --> 00:07:38.891
-Running around, having
a good time as a super fan.

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:42.895
But when you see someone that
iconic, I think, actually appear

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:44.730
in real time in front of you,
it's --

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.232
-I also shout out to Victor
thinking, "You know what?

00:07:47.232 --> 00:07:50.035
I'm going to make this
the best possible situation.

00:07:50.035 --> 00:07:51.369
Get me the helmet."

00:07:51.369 --> 00:07:54.039
-Yeah, I would love
a signed helmet. So this is it.

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:58.410
Victor, if you would, sign
your helmet, send it to Seth.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.746
He'll get it to me.
Appreciate it. Appreciate that.

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:02.281
-He can have my address
but not yours?

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:04.449
-You'll have Seth's address
and not mine.

00:08:04.449 --> 00:08:07.052
No, but he could not have been
nicer about it.

00:08:07.052 --> 00:08:09.555
-Well, it only makes sense
for people to be nice to you.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:11.723
You are the nicest person I know
in show business.

00:08:11.723 --> 00:08:12.892
Kenan Thompson, everybody.

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:15.561
"Kenan," Monday nights
at 8:00 here on NBC.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:18.664
"SNL" is back this week
with host Willem Dafoe,

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:20.366
and musical guest Katy Perry.

